  "_exec_summary": [
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000123942,
      "SummaryText": "Grammer Logistics, Inc. - Apopka Transloading Facility is an LPG (propane and butane) railcar storage and transloading facility (specifically, railcar to truck tanker). This Risk Management Plan (RMP) covers the LPG railcar storage and transloading system (Program Level III) including storage of up to five (5) LPG railcars and one (1) or more transloading units.\n\nThe Grammer Logistics, Inc. - Apopka Transloading Facility complies with the U.S. Environmental Protection Agency's (EPA) accident prevention rules (40 CFR Part 68 Subpart D) and the Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) Process Safety Management (PSM) Standard (29 CFR Part 1910.119). This butane railcar storage and transloading system is designed, constructed, and maintained in accordance with NFPA #58 and the manufacturer's instructions. Railcars meet the U.S. Department of Transportation Federal Railroad Administration design requirements for pressurized tank cars.\n\nThis facility has never had an accident involving LPG which has resulted in deaths, injuries, property/environmental damage, evacuation or sheltering in-place.\n\nIn the event of an emergency involving the Grammer Logistics, Inc. - Apopka Transloading Facility butane railcar storage and transloading system, it is the policy of the facility to initially contact the Apopka Fire Department and request their assistance. The facility personnel are trained. Facility emergency response is coordinated with the fire department and Orange County Office of Emergency Management and/or the Central Florida LEPC. The primary hazardous materials response capabilities are provided by the Apopka Fire Department.\n\nImprovement actions to be considered primarily focus on site security and rail safety measures including continuing safety audits and safety inspections.\n\nNote: This facility initially began operations in approximately September 2020 and ceased operations in approximately October 2022. Between October 2022 and the resubmission date in  Oc"
    },
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 1,
      "FacilityID": 1000123942,
      "SummaryText": "tober 2025, no hazardous chemicals were storage at this facility. Prior to restarting operations in October 2025, a complete review of the PSM/RMP program was conducted and all programs were updated and verified to be suitable for current operations."
    }
  ]
